 "verdict": [
  "New: the morning #1 now adds the last PRE-MARKET trade before 8:00 ET, so it can run at 7:20 CT. In the backtest its #1 fell 5%+ open\u2192close on 52% / 54% of sessions (development / confirmation) vs 49% / 52% for the close-only model, averaging \u22124.9% / \u22125.4% (close-only \u22123.9% / \u22123.5%); after each pick's estimated cost +1.5% / +1.6% per trade at $10K.",
  "Paired day by day with the close-only model: +1.0% per trade in development (90% interval \u22121.1% to +3.1%) and +1.9% in confirmation (\u22120.5% to +4.3%) \u2014 better in both windows, though each interval still includes zero.",
  "Why not the richer 9:00 ET version (which did better: 58% dumped, \u22124.9% in confirmation)? It needs the 8:05 CT run, and on 8 and 9 October that run could not finish before the bell while the Mac slept; Yahoo also stopped serving after-hours bars (17:00\u201318:59 ET) on 7 October. The pre-market-only version needs neither \u2014 and a feed check switches the morning model off (close-only scores) on any day its inputs look abnormal.",
  "The close-only model (the evening watchlist, and the morning fallback) still finds dumps \u2014 50% of its #1s fell 5%+ open\u2192close vs 9% for the average name (point-in-time backtest), averaging \u22123.4% before costs.",
  "But these are thin stocks. With each pick's own estimated cost, its average trade nets \u22120.3% at $10K (estimated cost \u2248 3.7% round trip). The live tape records real bid/ask spreads to keep checking the cost model.",
  "Names that can take $500K\u2013$1M: the model still finds dump candidates at about 3\u20135\u00d7 the normal rate, but their average same-day move is too small to pay the costs at that size. No variant \u2014 stops, direction-aware ranking, the pre-market gap, liquid-only models \u2014 fixed that.",
  "20-session shorts in liquid names looked excellent (+4% to +12% per trade) on today's small-cap list, but that list over-represents stocks that had already collapsed. On a point-in-time universe the result is mixed and statistically indistinguishable from zero (about 11 independent trades per period). Not confirmed, not shipped.",
  "So the honest answer to \u201c$500K\u2013$1M without losing accuracy\u201d is no \u2014 not with these signals and free data. GRAVITY shows every pick's capacity, cost at your size and breakeven, so you can size each trade to what the stock can actually absorb."
 ],
